Privacy Policy for Midnight Rig: Neon Haul
Last Updated: November 11, 2026
Effective Date: November 11, 2026
This Privacy Policy applies to the mobile game Midnight Rig: Neon Haul (the "Application" or "Game"), package identifier com.midnightrig.neonhaul, developed and published as a commercial / ad-supported title (the "Service").
We respect your privacy. This document outlines how data is collected, used, and protected when you install, play, and interact with Midnight Rig: Neon Haul.
1. Information We Do Not Collect
Midnight Rig: Neon Haul is designed to minimize data collection:
No User Accounts: You are not required to create an account, log in, or provide personal details (such as your legal name, physical address, phone number, or email address) to play the game.
No Precise Geolocation: The game does not access your device’s GPS, cell tower location, or fine location sensors. (All truck navigation and GPS beacons in the game represent simulated, fictional road coordinates).
No Access to Sensitive Hardware: The game does not access your microphone, camera, contacts, photos, or file system outside its own sandbox.
2. Information Collected by Third-Party Services (Advertising & Analytics)
To keep Midnight Rig: Neon Haul free to play, the game integrates third-party advertising networks (such as Google AdMob and/or AppLovin / MAX) to serve optional rewarded video lifelines and interstitial transitions.
These third-party SDKs may automatically collect and process certain non-personally identifiable information, including:
Device Identifiers: Google Advertising ID (GAID / AAID), IP address, and unique pseudonymous device identifiers.
Hardware & Software Specifications: Device model, manufacturer, operating system version, screen resolution, system language, and network carrier type.
Ad Interaction Data: Ad view duration, click-throughs, impressions, and completion events for rewarded lifelines.
These third parties process data in accordance with their respective privacy policies:
Google Play Services & AdMob: https://policies.google.com/privacy
AppLovin: https://www.applovin.com/privacy/
3. Device Permissions Used
Midnight Rig: Neon Haul requests only the minimum device permissions required for gameplay functionality:
android.permission.VIBRATE: Triggers tactile haptic feedback when shifting gears, stomping the pneumatic air brake, or colliding with curbs.
android.permission.WAKE_LOCK: Keeps the phone display illuminated while actively maneuvering and driving the truck, preventing unwanted screen dimming during gameplay.
android.permission.INTERNET & ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE: Required solely to stream third-party ad inventory (rewarded videos and interstitials) and verify network connectivity.
4. Local Data Storage
All game state—including unlocked contract tiers, driving preferences (such as your chosen D-pad layout: Centered, Split, Left, or Right), sound volume levels, and high scores—is stored locally on your device (via HTML5 localStorage / application preferences).
This data is never transmitted to our private servers and is erased if you clear the app’s cache or uninstall the game.
5. Children’s Privacy (COPPA Compliance)
Midnight Rig: Neon Haul is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect or solicit personal information from children under 13.
If you are a parent or guardian and believe that your child has provided personal information or that an integrated ad provider has inadvertently collected data from a child under 13, please contact us immediately at asterdaye@gmail.com, and we will take immediate steps to remove such information.
6. Your Rights and Opting Out of Targeted Advertising
You have control over how advertising data is used on your Android device:
Reset or Delete Advertising ID: Open your Android device’s Settings 
 Google 
 Ads, where you can reset your Advertising ID or toggle on "Delete Advertising ID" to prevent personalized ad tracking across all apps.
GDPR / CCPA / CPRA Notice: If you reside in the European Economic Area (EEA), the United Kingdom, or California, you are entitled to access, rectify, or request deletion of data held by third-party ad networks under applicable data protection laws. Because we do not store personal profiles on our own servers, requests regarding advertising identifiers can be handled via the third-party privacy portals linked in Section 2.
7. Security
We take the security of your device seriously. Midnight Rig: Neon Haul operates strictly within the standard Android application sandbox, and all network transmissions initiated by third-party ad SDKs are encrypted in transit via Transport Layer Security (HTTPS).
8. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in regulatory standards or game updates. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last Updated" date. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
